      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "Follow these strict rules when generating code: do not use loops or arrays (such as `for`, `forEach`, or `map`), do not use function parameters, and avoid all logical operators including NOT (`!`), AND (`&&`), and OR (`||`). Do not use class toggling or `querySelector` to find child elements; instead, modify styles directly on the buttons (e.g., `heartButton1.style.fill = \"black\"`) and do not use `classList`. Write separate, named arrow functions for each button and handle each one individually without abstraction. Use explicit boolean comparisons (e.g., `variable === false`) and maintain separate variables (`favorites1`, `favorites2`, etc.) to track state. All logic must be written using simple `if/else` statements that map directly to the flowchart, and every click event must update the `favoritesCount` using arithmetic and then immediately update the `favoritesCountBubble.textContent`/=. You must write complete code for all four buttons (heartButton1, heartButton2, heartButton3, heartButton4); do not provide a single example or partial implementation.\n"
      }
